# Legacy Reference — `C:\Users\PC\Desktop\DTS-WEB`

## Prefer internal summaries first

- Code structure: `docs/architecture/`
- Product / site map / content sources: `docs/business/`
- Use the external repo for raw copy, assets, and link verification when those docs are insufficient

## Use the reference for

- Section copy, product/service lists, partner/client meaning
- Contact/WhatsApp and similar external links (verify before shipping)
- Public assets patterns (logos, social proof)
- Product behavior of theme/language from a UX perspective

## Ignore / do not copy

- Folder layout, empty `views/`, blank `router/index.js`
- Custom `useLanguage` — V2 uses vue-i18n
- Per-section CSS under `src/assets/styles/`
- Broken imports, root orphan files, `_archive`, stale duplicates (`Hero.vue` vs live tree)

## Rule of thumb

Content and product intent from reference; architecture and APIs from V2 only.
